WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:50.967
THE APARTMENT JOB

3
00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:01.394
<i>Then will you let me be the keeper</i>

4
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.229
of your vault?

5
00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:07.442
You are the perfect man
to take on that position.

6
00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:11.237
MR. SON. SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

7
00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:14.699
Yes?

8
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.201
<i>Hey. Mr. Park.</i>

9
00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:18.995
Did you know
Park Yong-man was terminally ill?

10
00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:26.336
What did you just say?

11
00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.215
They say it's pancreatic cancer.
He has about three months left.

12
00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:33.218
<i>You'd better hurry</i>
<i>if you don't want him to die in there.</i>

13
00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:34.302
<i>Get the ten billion.</i>

14
00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:50.735
I'm bringing over the ten billion.
so release him.

15
00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:51.820
Right now!

16
00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:16.594
{\an8}<i>Uncle Hae-kang. here's a gift.</i>

17
00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.888
{\an8}This is amazing.

18
00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.974
You could be an artist. Gyeong-buk.

19
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:23.893
Is it really okay for me to have this?

20
00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.896
You're the head of our family. Uncle.

21
00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:29.482
<i>It seems like President Seo was taken out.</i>

22
00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:32.277
His entire family disappeared as well.

23
00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:35.738
<i>Then what did you see after failing?</i>

24
00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.866
This is my family.

25
00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.579
<i>We're a very happy family.</i>

26
00:02:45.915 --> 00:02:46.875
Gyeong-buk!

27
00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:56.259
Wow!

28
00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:58.344
<i>People.</i>

29
00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.430
<i>The people who are protecting me.</i>

30
00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.516
<i>and the people I should protect.</i>

31
00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:32.295
You crazy bastard. Are you kidding me?

32
00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:34.213
You said you'd bring the money.

33
00:03:34.297 --> 00:03:36.049
You were bringing the ten billion!

34
00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:39.802
That's why I had him moved

35
00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:43.097
to the hospital at this late hour.

36
00:03:43.181 --> 00:03:44.724
Do you think I'm playing around?

37
00:03:44.807 --> 00:03:47.268
All right. You just watch.

38
00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:50.772
You're the one
who's killing Park Yong-man.

39
00:03:50.855 --> 00:03:52.565
Understand? You jerk.

40
00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:55.818
What the hell are you doing? Let go of me.

41
00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.070
The medical bail comes first.

42
00:03:57.153 --> 00:04:00.323
I told you. our deal comes first!

43
00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.200
The situation's changed.

44
00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:05.954
As you know.
he doesn't have much time left.

45
00:04:06.037 --> 00:04:09.207
That's why you'd better bring the money.

46
00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.834
Bring me the ten billion. you asshole!

47
00:04:13.461 --> 00:04:15.296
Let go of me.

48
00:04:17.006 --> 00:04:18.508
You'd better hurry.

49
00:04:19.842 --> 00:04:21.886
because that ten billion you want

50
00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.515
is on borrowed time too.

51
00:04:26.182 --> 00:04:27.058
Understand?

52
00:04:37.068 --> 00:04:39.112
{\an8}PATIENT PARK YONG-MAN

53
00:05:03.594 --> 00:05:04.846
Yong-man.

54
00:05:05.513 --> 00:05:07.223
Hang in there.

55
00:05:10.852 --> 00:05:12.645
Hang in there just a while longer.

56
00:05:13.396 --> 00:05:14.314
Just a little more.

57
00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:38.880
GUNAM TAESAN FACILITY MANAGER

58
00:05:46.804 --> 00:05:48.639
They received the money.

59
00:05:50.475 --> 00:05:53.519
He needed the ten billion won
for his old boss.

60
00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:57.398
but he didn't take my money?

61
00:05:58.107 --> 00:06:02.945
Don't you think he has the potential
to be my vault keeper?

62
00:06:03.446 --> 00:06:04.614
I've been meaning to ask…

63
00:06:05.239 --> 00:06:07.658
Why Park Hae-kang?

64
00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.835
Stupid dogs only care about food.

65
00:06:17.919 --> 00:06:20.630
But once a smart dog is trained.

66
00:06:21.297 --> 00:06:23.549
it stays loyal to its owner.

67
00:06:24.967 --> 00:06:28.888
He planted relics
to stop the new town construction

68
00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.766
and doubled the reserve fund fee.

69
00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.143
Park Hae-kang

70
00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:37.855
can see the bigger picture.

71
00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:45.571
I heard you delivered the money safely.

72
00:06:46.697 --> 00:06:47.824
Thank you so much.

73
00:06:48.616 --> 00:06:50.451
But what brings you here at this hour?

74
00:06:51.285 --> 00:06:52.495
I remembered

75
00:06:53.955 --> 00:06:57.458
that we haven't discussed
a very important matter.

76
00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:00.378
What exactly…

77
00:07:02.171 --> 00:07:04.674
You've acquired someone more capable
than President Seo.

78
00:07:05.383 --> 00:07:07.760
so you should

79
00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.389
compensate me accordingly.

80
00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.811
We haven't discussed your payment.

81
00:07:17.353 --> 00:07:19.897
I'm not a cheap guy.

82
00:07:19.981 --> 00:07:23.067
We almost had a serious misunderstanding.

83
00:07:24.527 --> 00:07:25.570
Mr. Park.

84
00:07:26.404 --> 00:07:27.697
How much do you want?

85
00:07:29.157 --> 00:07:29.991
Ten billion.

86
00:07:31.909 --> 00:07:33.369
I want ten billion won.

87
00:07:38.541 --> 00:07:41.127
I've already doubled the reserve fund fee.

88
00:07:41.752 --> 00:07:44.505
So about 600 million
will be added to the fund each month.

89
00:07:45.256 --> 00:07:46.090
I believe

90
00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:51.012
I'm worth at least ten billion.

91
00:07:58.936 --> 00:08:00.563
Okay. fine. Ten billion.

92
00:08:08.613 --> 00:08:13.326
THE APARTMENT JOB

93
00:08:18.456 --> 00:08:20.166
{\an8}Gyeong-nam. Je-gil. Big Guy.

94
00:08:23.461 --> 00:08:24.378
{\an8}Guys.

95
00:08:26.214 --> 00:08:27.089
{\an8}What?

96
00:08:29.258 --> 00:08:30.510
{\an8}Guys!

97
00:09:00.748 --> 00:09:03.251
Come on.
Make a wish and blow out the candles.

98
00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:05.920
How many candles is that?

99
00:09:06.003 --> 00:09:08.047
-One. two. three…
-He's an old man now.

100
00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.979
That was a success.

101
00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:25.273
-Were you surprised?
-He was surprised.

102
00:09:56.846 --> 00:09:57.722
Did you cry?

103
00:09:59.515 --> 00:10:01.100
No. I didn't cry.

104
00:10:01.183 --> 00:10:02.059
Never.

105
00:10:09.233 --> 00:10:12.236
They're the people
you want to protect. aren't they?

106
00:10:23.539 --> 00:10:26.584
Everyone's been saying that this place

107
00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:28.586
has an amazing sauna.

108
00:10:28.669 --> 00:10:29.920
Is it your first time here?

109
00:10:30.004 --> 00:10:31.213
Of course.

110
00:10:31.297 --> 00:10:32.673
I don't even live here.

111
00:10:33.174 --> 00:10:34.342
Then how do we get in?

112
00:10:34.925 --> 00:10:38.054
My friend lives here.

113
00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:39.764
I can just use her card.

114
00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.308
They don't even check your ID here.

115
00:10:42.391 --> 00:10:43.476
Come on.

116
00:10:44.352 --> 00:10:45.227
Unbelievable.

117
00:10:46.145 --> 00:10:49.482
So we've been paying the fees
while other people used our facilities.

118
00:10:49.565 --> 00:10:51.776
You saw the reserve fund fee. right?

119
00:10:51.859 --> 00:10:53.444
It's doubled now.

120
00:10:54.195 --> 00:10:56.447
But doesn't it seem like the elevators

121
00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.115
are working fine now?

122
00:10:59.116 --> 00:11:00.993
It does seem so.

123
00:11:01.702 --> 00:11:04.413
But they should still be replaced
before any accidents occur.

124
00:11:05.581 --> 00:11:06.874
Ridiculous.

125
00:11:06.957 --> 00:11:08.793
Whose is this? Let me have a sip.

126
00:11:11.087 --> 00:11:12.338
I can't believe it.

127
00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:15.508
Hey. did you know that there are people

128
00:11:15.591 --> 00:11:17.301
using our community sauna for free?

129
00:11:18.135 --> 00:11:19.929
But we have to use our cards to enter.

130
00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:21.347
Yes.

131
00:11:22.139 --> 00:11:23.599
But some were just entering

132
00:11:23.682 --> 00:11:26.602
right after someone used their card
to open the gate.

133
00:11:26.685 --> 00:11:29.021
And some are secretly lending them
to other people.

134
00:11:29.105 --> 00:11:32.149
I just heard there are rumors
that our sauna is good.

135
00:11:32.233 --> 00:11:34.652
My goodness.
Then they're using our sauna for free?

136
00:11:34.735 --> 00:11:37.029
No way. It's not even that expensive.

137
00:11:37.113 --> 00:11:39.615
I just saw some people entering like that.

138
00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:43.160
If that's true.
this needs to be made public.

139
00:11:44.829 --> 00:11:47.289
REPORTING FACILITY MISUSE

140
00:11:54.463 --> 00:11:55.297
Please. eat.

141
00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:57.716
You probably had dinner.

142
00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.802
so I prepared some light snacks.

143
00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.097
We should make a toast.

144
00:12:04.515 --> 00:12:06.434
but the guest of honor isn't here yet.

145
00:12:07.101 --> 00:12:08.436
Please wait a moment.

146
00:12:09.186 --> 00:12:11.355
Is someone else coming?

147
00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:16.944
He's here.

148
00:12:21.157 --> 00:12:22.032
Say hello.

149
00:12:22.783 --> 00:12:25.411
Today's guest of honor. Park Hae-kang.

150
00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:27.955
You're here today

151
00:12:28.789 --> 00:12:31.292
thanks to Mr. Park.

152
00:12:33.586 --> 00:12:35.045
Say hello.

153
00:12:41.093 --> 00:12:42.303
Please. sit.

154
00:12:42.803 --> 00:12:43.762
Sit down.

155
00:12:45.598 --> 00:12:46.474
Go on.

156
00:12:52.104 --> 00:12:53.439
<i>So these two</i>

157
00:12:54.023 --> 00:12:56.066
<i>really were working for Lee Chung-won.</i>

158
00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.068
When President Seo was alive.

159
00:12:58.152 --> 00:13:00.613
I never got to prepare
a gathering like this.

160
00:13:00.696 --> 00:13:03.908
<i>Just how much influence does he have?</i>

161
00:13:03.991 --> 00:13:06.118
But we're a family now.

162
00:13:06.744 --> 00:13:09.830
So let's all line our pockets together.

163
00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:16.003
I'm joking.

164
00:13:17.713 --> 00:13:19.507
Why aren't you laughing?

165
00:13:22.801 --> 00:13:26.805
I'm just giving these out to you
because I'm in a good mood today.

166
00:13:26.889 --> 00:13:28.182
Hand them out.

167
00:13:40.903 --> 00:13:44.198
I gave you all an equal amount.

168
00:13:47.743 --> 00:13:48.786
See?

169
00:13:49.286 --> 00:13:52.164
Receiving gifts lightens the mood.
doesn't it?

170
00:13:52.248 --> 00:13:54.792
All right. How about a toast?

171
00:13:57.169 --> 00:13:58.712
Raise your glasses.

172
00:14:00.756 --> 00:14:01.799
Cheers.

173
00:14:02.383 --> 00:14:03.384
Cheers.

174
00:14:15.521 --> 00:14:16.355
I…

175
00:14:18.357 --> 00:14:21.944
You should have at least
told us in advance.

176
00:14:23.737 --> 00:14:25.030
{\an8}It hasn't been long.

177
00:14:26.323 --> 00:14:27.575
What about you two?

178
00:14:28.117 --> 00:14:30.536
Ever since we started working here…

179
00:14:30.619 --> 00:14:31.745
Mr. Choi.

180
00:14:37.418 --> 00:14:40.004
{\an8}Then I'll look forward
to working with you. sir.

181
00:14:49.388 --> 00:14:51.974
Were you faking a family to do this?

182
00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:53.767
What?

183
00:14:54.518 --> 00:14:55.936
Ha-jeong. what are you doing?

184
00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.771
I'm coming.

185
00:14:58.314 --> 00:14:59.815
You should stop this right now.

186
00:15:09.742 --> 00:15:12.870
When did Mr. Lee
get Park Hae-kang on his side too?

187
00:15:14.455 --> 00:15:16.081
Whatever.

188
00:15:16.832 --> 00:15:19.209
It's not easy for people like us
to earn money.

189
00:15:20.169 --> 00:15:21.629
You know very well

190
00:15:21.712 --> 00:15:23.881
how much education costs. don't you?

191
00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:26.008
Yes.

192
00:15:27.676 --> 00:15:31.639
All I want
is to live quietly without any trouble

193
00:15:31.722 --> 00:15:34.892
until my kid graduates
from school in Canada.

194
00:15:36.226 --> 00:15:37.603
So please cooperate. Ha-jeong.

195
00:15:38.854 --> 00:15:39.772
Okay.

196
00:15:39.855 --> 00:15:42.191
I'll get going now. Mr. Choi.

197
00:15:42.274 --> 00:15:43.859
Right. Bye.

198
00:15:57.539 --> 00:15:58.707
Kang Ha-ri.

199
00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:01.168
Quit that stand-in gig. right now.

200
00:16:02.294 --> 00:16:03.379
What?

201
00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:05.756
Do you even know what you've been doing?

202
00:16:05.839 --> 00:16:08.133
Do you know what kind of man
Park Hae-kang is?

203
00:16:09.343 --> 00:16:12.096
What about him? What's this about?

204
00:16:13.138 --> 00:16:15.391
You really are clueless. aren't you?

205
00:16:17.643 --> 00:16:19.186
What's gotten into her?

206
00:16:19.269 --> 00:16:20.521
Are you drunk?

207
00:16:43.877 --> 00:16:45.629
TRANSACTION LEDGER

208
00:16:52.136 --> 00:16:55.014
TRANSFERRED TO PRESIDENT SEO

209
00:17:09.903 --> 00:17:11.780
-Is it airtight?
-Yes.

210
00:17:12.614 --> 00:17:15.743
No one can tell by looking at the ledger.

211
00:17:15.826 --> 00:17:17.995
Of course. I know how skilled you are.

212
00:17:18.787 --> 00:17:20.581
Your sister's tuition is due soon. right?

213
00:17:23.709 --> 00:17:25.502
President Seo is very attentive.

214
00:17:34.428 --> 00:17:37.806
TRUE VALUE STATE
EXPENSE HISTORY

215
00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.808
FENCE REPAIRS
(MATERIAL COSTS OVERSTATED)

216
00:17:39.892 --> 00:17:41.310
LEAK REPAIRS
(CHARGED EXTRA)

217
00:17:44.813 --> 00:17:46.815
<i>How did things end up like this?</i>

218
00:17:52.446 --> 00:17:54.907
Attention. everyone.
We're all getting the same thing.

219
00:17:57.201 --> 00:17:58.660
Rotisserie chicken. 15 centimeters.

220
00:17:58.744 --> 00:18:00.537
grain bread with American cheese.

221
00:18:00.621 --> 00:18:02.039
heated in the oven.

222
00:18:02.122 --> 00:18:03.290
and leave out the pickles.

223
00:18:03.373 --> 00:18:05.417
Low-sugar onion and barbecue sauce.

224
00:18:06.168 --> 00:18:07.795
One. two. three. four. five…

225
00:18:08.545 --> 00:18:09.755
Six of them. please.

226
00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:12.216
-There are five of us. Why six?
-Yeah. why?

227
00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:15.427
It's tasty. so I'm getting two.

228
00:18:15.511 --> 00:18:16.804
Then one more for me.

229
00:18:16.887 --> 00:18:17.930
Me too. For Gyeong-buk.

230
00:18:18.013 --> 00:18:18.931
Me too.

231
00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:22.768
I need to send some to my family.
so five more.

232
00:18:22.851 --> 00:18:24.019
With all the ingredients.

233
00:18:27.356 --> 00:18:28.649
Fifteen. then.

234
00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:30.651
Fifteen?

235
00:18:32.277 --> 00:18:35.114
What? You met with the two of them?

236
00:18:35.656 --> 00:18:37.616
That's nerve-racking.

237
00:18:37.699 --> 00:18:39.993
Inviting you all together
to skim the fund…

238
00:18:40.077 --> 00:18:42.913
He really is something. isn't he?

239
00:18:42.996 --> 00:18:44.414
But the thing is… Come closer.

240
00:18:46.291 --> 00:18:47.584
The accounting manager

241
00:18:47.668 --> 00:18:50.337
knows that we're a fake family.

242
00:18:52.339 --> 00:18:53.173
How does she know?

243
00:18:53.257 --> 00:18:55.384
I'll get rid of her after I finish these.

244
00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:57.761
I'll hold back.

245
00:18:58.387 --> 00:18:59.513
She has a dirty secret too.

246
00:18:59.596 --> 00:19:03.100
so she won't be able to tell people
that we're a fake family.

247
00:19:03.183 --> 00:19:06.436
Ms. Jang. and now the accounting manager…

248
00:19:06.937 --> 00:19:08.689
Everyone will find out at this rate.

249
00:19:09.523 --> 00:19:12.568
We'll leave as soon as I get
the ten billion from him.

250
00:19:12.651 --> 00:19:13.610
-Yes. Boss.
-Yes. Boss.

251
00:19:14.194 --> 00:19:15.779
-Let's eat.
-Yes. Boss.

252
00:19:17.656 --> 00:19:20.033
Mr. Choi. you should see this.

253
00:19:20.534 --> 00:19:22.619
What is it this time?

254
00:19:23.245 --> 00:19:25.080
A complaint about people
using our facilities.

255
00:19:25.164 --> 00:19:26.832
REPORTING FACILITY MISUSE

256
00:19:27.457 --> 00:19:30.210
{\an8}"Let's find out who they are
and shame them"?

257
00:19:30.294 --> 00:19:33.046
{\an8}"Freeloaders." "Free sauna."

258
00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.132
{\an8}"Security is too lax"?

259
00:19:35.716 --> 00:19:38.051
{\an8}They're proposing
a facial recognition system.

260
00:19:38.135 --> 00:19:42.639
Why is this leading to talk
about a facial recognition system?

261
00:19:42.723 --> 00:19:43.932
-No.
-No.

262
00:19:46.143 --> 00:19:47.811
Why would we spend needless money

263
00:19:47.895 --> 00:19:51.106
just because
of a few irresponsible people?

264
00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.983
I'm against this.

265
00:19:53.066 --> 00:19:55.652
I think so as well.

266
00:19:56.278 --> 00:20:00.240
but more and more people
are agreeing to the idea.

267
00:20:01.158 --> 00:20:02.534
They want to use the reserve fund?

268
00:20:04.077 --> 00:20:05.787
-Yes.
-No…

269
00:20:05.871 --> 00:20:06.830
I mean…

270
00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.791
All we have to do is find the people

271
00:20:09.875 --> 00:20:12.461
who are misusing our facilities
and give them a warning.

272
00:20:13.086 --> 00:20:15.088
Yes. that will be enough.

273
00:20:15.172 --> 00:20:17.966
Let's find them and expose them.

274
00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:21.553
If rumors spread about them.
they'll be too ashamed to do it again.

275
00:20:22.054 --> 00:20:26.350
But how would we find them?

276
00:20:33.815 --> 00:20:36.818
All right. Good.

277
00:20:37.361 --> 00:20:38.904
{\an8}Stop. Right there.

278
00:20:38.987 --> 00:20:40.447
{\an8}The one with the pink basket.

279
00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:41.823
The elderly woman in the back.

280
00:20:41.907 --> 00:20:43.825
It's 12:54 and 7 seconds.

281
00:20:43.909 --> 00:20:45.827
…fifty-four and seven seconds.

282
00:20:45.911 --> 00:20:47.496
Check.

283
00:20:47.579 --> 00:20:49.081
It's Building 303. Unit 504.

284
00:20:49.164 --> 00:20:51.541
-Building 303…
-Unit 504.

285
00:20:51.625 --> 00:20:53.585
Unit 504. Okay. next.

286
00:20:56.296 --> 00:20:58.465
Still nothing from President Park?

287
00:20:58.548 --> 00:21:00.217
No. nothing.

288
00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:02.678
What about his brother?

289
00:21:02.761 --> 00:21:04.763
-Goodness!
-After drinking all that tea.

290
00:21:04.846 --> 00:21:05.973
he just ignores us?

291
00:21:06.056 --> 00:21:08.392
We even took his side
with the fee increase proposal.

292
00:21:08.475 --> 00:21:09.309
Right?

293
00:21:09.393 --> 00:21:12.896
This isn't right.
I didn't think he'd be like this.

294
00:21:13.855 --> 00:21:15.983
Things were better with President Seo.

295
00:21:16.066 --> 00:21:17.693
It was nice being a building rep.

296
00:21:18.193 --> 00:21:20.028
We have to pay for heating bills now.

297
00:21:21.697 --> 00:21:24.241
And we're not getting any kickbacks.
This is no fun.

298
00:21:25.951 --> 00:21:28.578
Do we have to keep working
as building reps like this?

299
00:21:28.662 --> 00:21:30.414
What choice do we have?

300
00:21:30.497 --> 00:21:32.457
It's not like we can
bring Park Hae-kang down.

301
00:21:34.793 --> 00:21:37.546
Isn't there some clever way

302
00:21:37.629 --> 00:21:40.215
to bring Park Hae-kang down?

303
00:21:40.799 --> 00:21:44.136
Things have been noisy lately
about stopping unauthorized use

304
00:21:44.219 --> 00:21:45.053
of our facilities.

305
00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:46.138
Unauthorized use?

306
00:21:46.221 --> 00:21:48.265
Then let's at least go and sit

307
00:21:48.348 --> 00:21:50.350
in the management office. not here.

308
00:21:50.434 --> 00:21:52.978
Good idea.
Let's hang around there instead.

309
00:21:53.061 --> 00:21:55.147
I'm sure we'll find something.

310
00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:56.481
-Let's go.
-Really?

311
00:21:56.565 --> 00:21:57.733
-Get up.
-Okay.

312
00:22:00.402 --> 00:22:02.821
-Hello.
-Hello.

313
00:22:02.904 --> 00:22:04.072
Hi. Yun-seo.

314
00:22:04.156 --> 00:22:05.198
Hello.

315
00:22:06.533 --> 00:22:07.826
Is something wrong?

316
00:22:07.909 --> 00:22:11.246
We just wanted to chat
with the residents a bit.

317
00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:13.832
And since you're all working so hard.

318
00:22:13.915 --> 00:22:16.043
-we want to hear about your troubles.
-Right.

319
00:22:16.126 --> 00:22:17.461
We want to chat over some tea.

320
00:22:18.086 --> 00:22:19.379
I see.

321
00:22:19.463 --> 00:22:21.423
But Mr. Choi and President Park

322
00:22:21.506 --> 00:22:23.508
just went to check the security footage.

323
00:22:23.592 --> 00:22:25.135
Don't mind us. You can keep working.

324
00:22:25.218 --> 00:22:27.054
We have lots of time on our hands.

325
00:22:27.137 --> 00:22:29.806
-I'll make the coffee myself.
-Sure.

326
00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:32.768
But where are all the other employees?

327
00:22:33.685 --> 00:22:35.604
Everyone's busy.

328
00:22:38.065 --> 00:22:39.024
Yes?

329
00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:41.359
No one's there?

330
00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:43.111
Hang on.

331
00:22:43.987 --> 00:22:47.115
Building 105. Unit 702.

332
00:22:47.199 --> 00:22:48.200
It's a rental unit.

333
00:22:48.283 --> 00:22:50.786
Looks like
only elderly residents live there.

334
00:22:51.369 --> 00:22:53.371
Why don't you check in the afternoon?

335
00:22:54.039 --> 00:22:55.248
Okay.

336
00:22:55.332 --> 00:22:56.833
Building 105?

337
00:22:57.334 --> 00:22:58.835
That's where I live. What's going on?

338
00:23:00.545 --> 00:23:03.173
We're visiting residents

339
00:23:03.256 --> 00:23:06.676
who misused the community facilities
and giving them a warning.

340
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:07.761
But they're not at home.

341
00:23:07.844 --> 00:23:10.555
I guess rental units
are misusing the facilities.

342
00:23:10.639 --> 00:23:13.266
They shouldn't do that
when they're living here for free.

343
00:23:13.850 --> 00:23:14.684
Pardon?

344
00:23:17.104 --> 00:23:18.313
No. it's not that--

345
00:23:18.396 --> 00:23:20.899
You seem busy. We'll come back next time.

346
00:23:21.399 --> 00:23:22.818
Right.

347
00:23:22.901 --> 00:23:25.028
I'll make my own coffee.

348
00:23:25.112 --> 00:23:26.655
-Bye.
-Bye.

349
00:23:27.364 --> 00:23:28.615
Bye…

350
00:23:34.454 --> 00:23:35.288
What is it?

351
00:23:35.372 --> 00:23:36.581
I think I got it.

352
00:23:36.665 --> 00:23:38.583
-What?
-Got what?

353
00:23:39.292 --> 00:23:40.168
A way…

354
00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:42.629
to drag Park Hae-kang down.

355
00:23:48.135 --> 00:23:49.302
What is it?

356
00:23:49.386 --> 00:23:51.888
MOST FACILITY MISUSE
COMES FROM RENTAL UNITS…

357
00:23:53.598 --> 00:23:57.185
{\an8}"Rental units should be limited
from using community facilities."

358
00:23:57.269 --> 00:23:59.604
"Rental unit beggars are the worst."

359
00:23:59.688 --> 00:24:01.773
"I'm struggling to pay
my mortgage interest."

360
00:24:01.857 --> 00:24:05.277
"It's infuriating how people
in the rental units have it so easy."

361
00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:07.237
"Reveal the rental units."

362
00:24:07.904 --> 00:24:10.031
{\an8}What kind of nonsense is this?

363
00:24:12.409 --> 00:24:13.577
What a load of crap.

364
00:24:16.246 --> 00:24:18.081
I'm sorry. sir.

365
00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:22.085
I was just asked
who lives in Building 105. Unit 702

366
00:24:22.169 --> 00:24:26.131
because they weren't answering their door.

367
00:24:27.257 --> 00:24:29.551
so I said it was a rental unit.

368
00:24:31.261 --> 00:24:33.847
But the building reps who came
overheard me.

369
00:24:33.930 --> 00:24:38.435
I don't know why this led
to all the talk about the rental units.

370
00:24:39.436 --> 00:24:41.229
It's not something to apologize to me for.

371
00:24:42.022 --> 00:24:44.691
But you should apologize directly to them.

372
00:24:45.400 --> 00:24:47.360
They're moving out.

373
00:24:49.237 --> 00:24:50.906
CAN'T YOU EVEN PAY FOR A SAUNA?

374
00:24:50.989 --> 00:24:53.200
<i>This is a social mix apartment complex.</i>

375
00:24:53.992 --> 00:24:56.786
<i>The rental units and owner-occupied units</i>
<i>are mixed here.</i>

376
00:24:56.870 --> 00:24:59.581
<i>so the residents</i>
<i>couldn't know which units were rented.</i>

377
00:25:00.665 --> 00:25:05.212
But the residents acted as though
they had been waiting for this to happen.

378
00:25:05.295 --> 00:25:08.131
so they seemed quite shocked.

379
00:25:08.965 --> 00:25:10.258
They said they just wanted

380
00:25:10.342 --> 00:25:14.012
to brag to their old neighbors
about living in a nice apartment complex.

381
00:25:14.721 --> 00:25:16.097
And here.

382
00:25:16.765 --> 00:25:20.977
They asked that this be used
for the apartment complex.

383
00:25:21.061 --> 00:25:22.812
And they apologized
for causing a commotion.

384
00:25:23.813 --> 00:25:25.357
It's the sauna fee.

385
00:25:37.285 --> 00:25:38.245
Here.

386
00:25:38.328 --> 00:25:39.913
Try another color too.

387
00:25:41.122 --> 00:25:42.666
Next color…

388
00:25:42.749 --> 00:25:44.042
Good.

389
00:25:44.125 --> 00:25:45.335
You're so smart.

390
00:25:45.418 --> 00:25:46.419
Draw one at the bottom.

391
00:25:46.503 --> 00:25:48.588
Wow. that's so cool.

392
00:25:48.672 --> 00:25:50.257
That's amazing.

393
00:25:50.340 --> 00:25:51.466
So cute.

394
00:25:52.676 --> 00:25:53.760
Who is this?

395
00:25:55.095 --> 00:25:56.805
-That's a nice rainbow.
-Is this Mom?

396
00:25:56.888 --> 00:25:59.808
What on earth are you doing right now?

397
00:26:01.601 --> 00:26:03.895
They're water-soluble crayons.

398
00:26:03.979 --> 00:26:05.355
It'll get washed away in the rain.

399
00:26:06.273 --> 00:26:09.442
This is still a public place.

400
00:26:09.526 --> 00:26:13.530
Are you seriously drawing
on a public building?

401
00:26:14.114 --> 00:26:15.573
We weren't…

402
00:26:15.657 --> 00:26:16.700
Oh gosh.

403
00:26:16.783 --> 00:26:20.036
Why do people here
have no sense of responsibility?

404
00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:23.039
Are you teaching your kids that it's okay

405
00:26:23.123 --> 00:26:24.666
to vandalize public property?

406
00:26:24.749 --> 00:26:27.877
We just told you
that it'll get washed away in the rain.

407
00:26:28.670 --> 00:26:30.046
Look.

408
00:26:30.130 --> 00:26:33.133
There's no forecast of rain
for a whole week.

409
00:26:33.216 --> 00:26:36.386
Then we can just spray water on it.

410
00:26:36.469 --> 00:26:37.887
And you can talk quietly.

411
00:26:37.971 --> 00:26:39.806
Why are you shouting
when there are kids here?

412
00:26:39.889 --> 00:26:43.268
So I guess you do feel embarrassed
getting called out in front of them.

413
00:26:43.351 --> 00:26:46.479
It's okay for kids to scribble sometimes.
and we said we'd erase it.

414
00:26:47.063 --> 00:26:48.565
You said the rain would wash it away.

415
00:26:48.648 --> 00:26:53.361
That means you had no intention
of erasing it before it rained.

416
00:26:53.445 --> 00:26:56.072
You should be the ones
stopping your kids from doing that.

417
00:26:56.156 --> 00:26:57.866
but you're doing it with them?

418
00:26:57.949 --> 00:27:00.285
Are you thoughtless or ill-mannered?

419
00:27:00.368 --> 00:27:01.578
Or just uneducated?

420
00:27:01.661 --> 00:27:02.620
You're unbelievable!

421
00:27:02.704 --> 00:27:04.414
-Did you hear that?
-Ma'am.

422
00:27:04.497 --> 00:27:05.707
You're being…

423
00:27:06.624 --> 00:27:07.876
What?

424
00:27:07.959 --> 00:27:09.711
Am I wrong?

425
00:27:09.794 --> 00:27:13.590
You young mothers
should have some sense of ownership!

426
00:27:13.673 --> 00:27:15.925
Is this really that big of a deal?

427
00:27:16.009 --> 00:27:18.678
We all have a sense of ownership!
We own our units!

428
00:27:18.762 --> 00:27:19.888
I'm an owner too!

429
00:27:19.971 --> 00:27:21.556
Right. Good for you.

430
00:27:21.639 --> 00:27:24.476
If you took out massive loans
to become owners

431
00:27:24.559 --> 00:27:26.561
of apartments like this.

432
00:27:26.644 --> 00:27:28.313
you should be thinking

433
00:27:28.396 --> 00:27:31.358
about educating your kids
and helping raise the property value.

434
00:27:31.441 --> 00:27:33.902
If rumors spread
about how bratty the kids are here.

435
00:27:33.985 --> 00:27:35.737
the prices will drop!

436
00:27:35.820 --> 00:27:37.072
-Hey!
-Hey!

437
00:27:37.822 --> 00:27:40.367
What? Why?

438
00:27:41.368 --> 00:27:42.285
-Gosh.
-My goodness.

439
00:27:42.369 --> 00:27:43.495
What's with that woman?

440
00:27:43.578 --> 00:27:44.871
As if she doesn't have any loans.

441
00:27:44.954 --> 00:27:46.873
Isn't there a way to find out?

442
00:27:46.956 --> 00:27:47.791
Is there?

443
00:27:47.874 --> 00:27:49.459
We can check the property registry.

444
00:27:49.542 --> 00:27:51.586
Anyone can view it
if you know the address.

445
00:27:51.669 --> 00:27:52.629
Really?

446
00:27:53.296 --> 00:27:55.465
She's in Building 112. right?

447
00:27:55.548 --> 00:27:56.591
Yes. Unit 902.

448
00:27:56.674 --> 00:27:59.177
We don't need to go that far.

449
00:27:59.260 --> 00:28:01.137
It's true that we drew
on a public building.

450
00:28:01.221 --> 00:28:03.348
We know it was our fault.

451
00:28:03.431 --> 00:28:05.767
but she was going on
about a sense of ownership

452
00:28:05.850 --> 00:28:07.977
and calling our kids brats
over something so trivial.

453
00:28:08.061 --> 00:28:10.438
We didn't need to hear
such harsh comments.

454
00:28:10.522 --> 00:28:11.481
You're right.

455
00:28:12.315 --> 00:28:14.484
She speaks so harshly.

456
00:28:14.567 --> 00:28:16.361
-She was spewing nonsense.
-Yeah.

457
00:28:17.320 --> 00:28:19.989
Let's sleep early today. okay?

458
00:28:20.698 --> 00:28:22.951
Mom. what's a loan?

459
00:28:25.787 --> 00:28:26.663
Well…

460
00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:31.960
It's when you borrow money from a bank
when you don't have enough.

461
00:28:32.585 --> 00:28:34.087
Do we not have money?

462
00:28:34.921 --> 00:28:35.880
What?

463
00:28:35.964 --> 00:28:38.049
That lady earlier

464
00:28:38.133 --> 00:28:40.218
said we had a huge loan.

465
00:28:46.141 --> 00:28:47.434
No. well…

466
00:28:49.436 --> 00:28:51.020
It's not huge.

467
00:28:52.814 --> 00:28:53.898
We have a bit.

468
00:28:54.482 --> 00:28:55.692
Just a little.

469
00:28:55.775 --> 00:28:58.611
Hardly anyone buys an apartment
without a loan.

470
00:28:59.112 --> 00:29:00.780
She spoke as if she didn't.

471
00:29:05.702 --> 00:29:07.120
Should I check?

472
00:29:11.541 --> 00:29:13.877
What unit was she in again?

473
00:29:14.794 --> 00:29:16.796
{\an8}Building 112. Unit 902…

474
00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:18.298
{\an8}PROPERTY REGISTRY

475
00:29:20.425 --> 00:29:21.342
Oh my gosh.

476
00:29:33.646 --> 00:29:36.191
You have to do well today. okay?

477
00:29:36.941 --> 00:29:39.152
That sapling incident and the drawings…

478
00:29:39.235 --> 00:29:40.945
Remember everything she put us through.

479
00:29:41.029 --> 00:29:42.238
Too many to count.

480
00:29:42.322 --> 00:29:44.699
It's just ridiculous.

481
00:29:44.783 --> 00:29:47.786
Make sure she won't even dare
to say a thing.

482
00:29:47.869 --> 00:29:49.412
-Okay?
-Take her down a peg.

483
00:29:49.496 --> 00:29:50.955
You can do it.

484
00:29:51.039 --> 00:29:52.540
-We're relying on you.
-You can do it.

485
00:29:59.214 --> 00:30:01.341
TRUE VALUE STATE
RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION MEETING

486
00:30:03.510 --> 00:30:07.305
Let us begin
the residents' association meeting.

487
00:30:07.388 --> 00:30:09.349
Today's agenda

488
00:30:09.432 --> 00:30:12.977
is how to prevent misuse
of the community center.

489
00:30:13.061 --> 00:30:14.187
Excuse me.

490
00:30:16.272 --> 00:30:18.650
Before starting the meeting.

491
00:30:18.733 --> 00:30:21.277
there's something I thought
you should know in advance.

492
00:30:21.361 --> 00:30:23.112
Let me announce something.

493
00:30:23.196 --> 00:30:24.614
For the past month.

494
00:30:24.697 --> 00:30:29.160
President Park and I have been staying up
all night reviewing security footage.

495
00:30:29.244 --> 00:30:33.289
checking the residents who have been
misusing the community center.

496
00:30:33.373 --> 00:30:37.168
We've identified a total of 108 cases.

497
00:30:37.252 --> 00:30:41.589
Four of them were from rental units.

498
00:30:41.673 --> 00:30:44.592
and the remaining 104

499
00:30:44.676 --> 00:30:47.387
were from purchased units.

500
00:30:48.513 --> 00:30:49.806
-Purchased units?
-What?

501
00:30:49.889 --> 00:30:51.891
That's way more than the rental units.

502
00:30:51.975 --> 00:30:54.310
The rental units
must have been pretty frustrated.

503
00:30:54.394 --> 00:30:56.855
Which purchased units
were being so thoughtless?

504
00:30:56.938 --> 00:30:58.147
Hang on.

505
00:30:58.231 --> 00:30:59.649
Are you sure about this?

506
00:31:00.275 --> 00:31:04.237
We visited each household to confirm this.
and they apologized.

507
00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:06.239
They promised not to do it again.

508
00:31:07.448 --> 00:31:08.908
So everyone.

509
00:31:08.992 --> 00:31:12.662
stop attacking the rental unit residents.

510
00:31:12.745 --> 00:31:15.248
and let us all get along--

511
00:31:15.331 --> 00:31:17.208
But. Ms. Jang.

512
00:31:18.084 --> 00:31:21.212
aren't you taking the rental units' side
because you're one too?

513
00:31:22.672 --> 00:31:23.923
-Rental unit?
-Ma'am.

514
00:31:24.007 --> 00:31:26.467
Everyone here lives
in an owner-occupied unit.

515
00:31:26.551 --> 00:31:28.428
Our management rules state

516
00:31:28.511 --> 00:31:30.763
that only those in owned units

517
00:31:31.389 --> 00:31:35.143
are able to participate
in the residents' association meetings.

518
00:31:35.226 --> 00:31:38.271
Then Ms. Jang should clearly leave.

519
00:31:38.354 --> 00:31:40.982
Because she doesn't own her unit.

520
00:31:42.025 --> 00:31:44.360
It's a rental unit
managed by the government.

521
00:31:46.404 --> 00:31:50.074
She always acted
like she had a say in everything.

522
00:31:50.158 --> 00:31:52.452
She spoke like that
when she's in a rental unit?

523
00:31:52.535 --> 00:31:54.537
-Wow.
-No wonder.

524
00:31:54.621 --> 00:31:56.623
She was always yelling at our kids.

525
00:31:56.706 --> 00:31:59.208
You were investigating stuff
and pretending to be a homeowner

526
00:31:59.292 --> 00:32:01.461
when you didn't have the authority?

527
00:32:01.544 --> 00:32:03.046
Hey.

528
00:32:03.713 --> 00:32:04.797
Pretending?

529
00:32:04.881 --> 00:32:08.635
That means she's been violating
our management rules.

530
00:32:08.718 --> 00:32:12.347
Residents from rental units
don't have the right to be here. so leave.

531
00:32:12.430 --> 00:32:13.598
She's right. Leave.

532
00:32:14.891 --> 00:32:16.184
Go.

533
00:32:18.436 --> 00:32:19.312
Get out!

534
00:32:19.395 --> 00:32:21.064
Hurry up and leave!

535
00:32:21.648 --> 00:32:22.649
Why?

536
00:32:26.152 --> 00:32:28.363
Why wouldn't I have the right?

537
00:32:30.448 --> 00:32:32.742
The government gave me the right

538
00:32:32.825 --> 00:32:36.913
to live here as if it were my own home
for 30 years without worrying.

539
00:32:37.497 --> 00:32:39.457
I don't pay as much as you.

540
00:32:39.540 --> 00:32:42.043
but I'm not living here for free.

541
00:32:42.627 --> 00:32:44.128
I pay the maintenance fees. the rent.

542
00:32:44.212 --> 00:32:46.547
and the government
pays for the reserve fund.

543
00:32:46.631 --> 00:32:49.926
I'm paying to live here too.
Why shouldn't I have the right?

544
00:32:52.387 --> 00:32:53.930
I don't own my house.

545
00:32:54.013 --> 00:32:57.225
but I lived with a bigger sense
of ownership than any of you.

546
00:32:58.142 --> 00:32:59.894
<i>It wasn't just my own house.</i>

547
00:32:59.978 --> 00:33:02.647
<i>I cleaned all around</i>
<i>the apartment complex.</i>

548
00:33:03.231 --> 00:33:04.607
<i>treating it as my own home.</i>

549
00:33:04.691 --> 00:33:09.404
Was anyone here more invested
in True Value's affairs than I was?

550
00:33:09.487 --> 00:33:10.530
Anyone?

551
00:33:11.948 --> 00:33:14.450
Building reps. say something.

552
00:33:14.534 --> 00:33:15.952
You have the title.

553
00:33:16.035 --> 00:33:19.247
but did any of you even care
if any electricity was being wasted

554
00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:21.582
or if any facilities were broken.

555
00:33:21.666 --> 00:33:24.210
causing danger to the residents?

556
00:33:24.293 --> 00:33:26.921
Did any of you even care
about things like that?

557
00:33:27.005 --> 00:33:29.173
Even so.

558
00:33:29.257 --> 00:33:30.925
you're still from a rental unit.

559
00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:33.845
Do I need some kind of qualification

560
00:33:33.928 --> 00:33:36.723
to want to make
the apartment complex I live in

561
00:33:38.141 --> 00:33:40.435
a better place?

562
00:33:41.561 --> 00:33:45.148
Just because
I'm a tiny bit poorer than you.

563
00:33:45.231 --> 00:33:48.234
am I supposed to shut up
and keep my head down?

564
00:33:49.277 --> 00:33:50.820
Management rules?

565
00:33:51.320 --> 00:33:54.824
What kind of stupid management rules
are like that?

566
00:33:56.826 --> 00:33:57.785
How…

567
00:33:58.911 --> 00:34:00.580
How could you treat people like that?

568
00:34:00.663 --> 00:34:02.540
Oh. whatever.

569
00:34:02.623 --> 00:34:04.333
It's still against the rules.

570
00:34:04.417 --> 00:34:05.752
It's clearly stated.

571
00:34:05.835 --> 00:34:08.129
-This is wrong.
-We should follow procedure.

572
00:34:08.212 --> 00:34:10.048
-We should stick to…
-Stop.

573
00:34:59.806 --> 00:35:01.390
Sir! Be careful!

574
00:35:01.474 --> 00:35:02.850
Be careful not to scratch anything.

575
00:35:02.934 --> 00:35:04.811
-To the right.
-This way.

576
00:35:04.894 --> 00:35:06.479
Don't put it there.

577
00:35:06.562 --> 00:35:10.483
You have to place them on the mat.
Don't put them on the floor.

578
00:35:10.983 --> 00:35:12.985
You moved to a nice place. ma'am.

579
00:35:14.654 --> 00:35:16.697
It's a new apartment.

580
00:35:18.491 --> 00:35:20.076
No need for such formality.

581
00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:23.663
I really

582
00:35:24.288 --> 00:35:27.416
don't need to worry about a house anymore!

583
00:35:31.212 --> 00:35:35.800
This will be my home for 30 years.

584
00:35:36.551 --> 00:35:40.263
So I guess I can call myself the owner.

585
00:35:43.015 --> 00:35:47.061
I'll be relying on you. elevator.

586
00:36:23.055 --> 00:36:26.184
Did you have to bring that up
in front of everyone?

587
00:36:30.229 --> 00:36:32.648
It just seemed
like you wanted to humiliate her.

588
00:36:33.232 --> 00:36:34.358
Was that your intention?

589
00:36:36.903 --> 00:36:39.780
I was rash.

590
00:36:40.698 --> 00:36:42.074
I'm sorry.

591
00:36:44.076 --> 00:36:48.873
You should be apologizing
to Ms. Jang. not me.

592
00:36:54.462 --> 00:36:57.465
I really can't believe that Ms. Jang

593
00:36:57.548 --> 00:36:59.133
is in a rental unit.

594
00:37:00.718 --> 00:37:05.056
You should've checked when she applied
as a building rep candidate.

595
00:37:05.139 --> 00:37:07.767
You really didn't know. Mr. Choi?

596
00:37:08.392 --> 00:37:09.602
I didn't.

597
00:37:10.102 --> 00:37:12.772
She was meddling in everything.

598
00:37:12.855 --> 00:37:14.815
so of course I thought she owned her unit.

599
00:37:14.899 --> 00:37:17.151
Who would've imagined
it was a rental unit?

600
00:37:17.235 --> 00:37:19.028
She stuck her nose into everything.

601
00:37:19.987 --> 00:37:22.615
Sang-tae. don't talk about her like that.

602
00:37:23.199 --> 00:37:26.035
How can you say that
after hearing everything she said?

603
00:37:27.203 --> 00:37:28.996
I was just…

604
00:37:29.080 --> 00:37:33.042
Ms. Jang even went around
scraping gum off the ground.

605
00:37:33.125 --> 00:37:34.168
Yeah.

606
00:37:34.252 --> 00:37:38.381
Ms. Jang loves and cares for True Value

607
00:37:38.464 --> 00:37:40.091
more than any of the owners.

608
00:37:52.103 --> 00:37:52.937
Mom.

609
00:37:53.479 --> 00:37:55.106
I might get a scholarship this semester.

610
00:37:56.148 --> 00:37:57.066
Okay.

611
00:38:15.710 --> 00:38:16.544
Mom.

612
00:38:17.086 --> 00:38:19.255
Even if we don't own this house.

613
00:38:20.464 --> 00:38:22.800
I've been really happy living here.

614
00:38:25.428 --> 00:38:28.222
So I wondered why I was so happy.

615
00:38:28.806 --> 00:38:31.183
and it was because of you. not this house.

616
00:38:32.560 --> 00:38:34.020
Because you're happy.

617
00:38:36.147 --> 00:38:36.981
Mom.

618
00:38:37.732 --> 00:38:39.233
The house isn't what's important.

619
00:38:40.901 --> 00:38:43.362
What matters is the happiness
of the people living there.

620
00:38:50.494 --> 00:38:51.829
I'm going to school now.

621
00:39:17.146 --> 00:39:18.481
This place is good.

622
00:39:19.982 --> 00:39:23.319
I'm sure you didn't call me
just to enjoy a nice meal.

623
00:39:23.819 --> 00:39:27.406
Why did you want to see me?

624
00:39:28.199 --> 00:39:31.535
Well. it's about
the Oman New Town project.

625
00:39:31.619 --> 00:39:34.914
We need to add more rental units
than we originally planned.

626
00:39:38.709 --> 00:39:40.920
-Why?
-Isn't it obvious?

627
00:39:41.003 --> 00:39:43.923
The VIP is pursuing policies
for ordinary people.

628
00:39:44.006 --> 00:39:46.717
so he wants to show off

629
00:39:46.801 --> 00:39:49.553
about adding more rental units
in the new town.

630
00:39:51.472 --> 00:39:53.224
Increasing housing supply

631
00:39:53.307 --> 00:39:57.937
while supporting vulnerable groups…

632
00:39:58.813 --> 00:40:00.064
It creates a good image.

633
00:40:06.862 --> 00:40:09.240
Did they replace the head chef?

634
00:40:09.323 --> 00:40:11.492
Why does it feel like I'm chewing on sand?

635
00:40:16.122 --> 00:40:17.623
Are you enjoying the food?

636
00:40:18.541 --> 00:40:20.459
You have quite the stomach.

637
00:40:20.543 --> 00:40:23.629
enjoying it
after the bomb you threw at me.

638
00:40:31.846 --> 00:40:32.930
Have a drink.

639
00:41:03.586 --> 00:41:07.006
An apartment costs a fortune.
and they want them for free?

640
00:41:08.174 --> 00:41:10.759
The government
is basically extorting money from me.

641
00:41:10.843 --> 00:41:12.470
Are they thugs or what?

642
00:41:14.054 --> 00:41:15.431
Damn rental units…

643
00:41:16.223 --> 00:41:18.100
I want to get rid of them all.

644
00:41:22.438 --> 00:41:24.607
TRUE VALUE FACILITY MANAGER

645
00:41:26.275 --> 00:41:27.359
What is it?

646
00:41:28.027 --> 00:41:31.155
You told me to report to you
every two days.

647
00:41:32.656 --> 00:41:33.782
Go on.

648
00:41:34.283 --> 00:41:36.494
<i>It's been kind of noisy here</i>

649
00:41:36.577 --> 00:41:40.664
with conflict between the rental units
and owned units

650
00:41:40.748 --> 00:41:43.167
surrounding the misuse
of community facilities.

651
00:41:43.250 --> 00:41:47.171
<i>President Park is probably getting</i>
<i>quite a headache because of this.</i>

652
00:41:48.047 --> 00:41:51.300
Rental units always seem
to be the problem.

653
00:41:58.891 --> 00:42:01.227
Give me back my apartments. you thieves!

654
00:42:01.310 --> 00:42:03.270
Are you thugs or what?

655
00:42:17.618 --> 00:42:19.245
Why did you call me at this hour?

656
00:42:19.870 --> 00:42:22.540
Drink this. It's good for your health.

657
00:42:31.298 --> 00:42:35.135
I heard you're having trouble
with the rental units.

658
00:42:36.220 --> 00:42:38.973
I'm pretty irritated because of them too.

659
00:42:40.432 --> 00:42:41.976
It's not really them.

660
00:42:42.059 --> 00:42:44.395
but the way people view them.

661
00:42:44.979 --> 00:42:47.106
Whatever the case.

662
00:42:47.189 --> 00:42:49.692
the rental units are the problem.

663
00:42:50.317 --> 00:42:51.443
The government

664
00:42:51.527 --> 00:42:54.154
wants my apartments for free.

665
00:42:54.697 --> 00:42:56.448
I gave them some. but they want more.

666
00:42:57.157 --> 00:42:58.784
They act as if they own them.

667
00:42:59.994 --> 00:43:03.706
They want to steal mine
and give them out as rental units.

668
00:43:04.290 --> 00:43:07.459
so it's only natural
for the owner to be pissed.

669
00:43:08.877 --> 00:43:11.547
The conflict between
the owned units and rental units…

670
00:43:12.423 --> 00:43:14.258
Right. Conflict.

671
00:43:15.884 --> 00:43:19.305
Should we just start a war between them?

672
00:43:19.888 --> 00:43:23.601
There's nothing more entertaining
than watching a fight.

673
00:43:25.394 --> 00:43:29.440
"Social mix." That's exactly the kind
of policy dreamed up by bureaucrats.

674
00:43:29.523 --> 00:43:32.067
People from different social classes
living together?

675
00:43:32.151 --> 00:43:34.403
Isn't that some kind of pipe dream?

676
00:43:35.237 --> 00:43:37.406
Let's be honest.

677
00:43:39.491 --> 00:43:42.828
Why don't we just mark the rental units

678
00:43:42.911 --> 00:43:44.538
with signs on their doors?

679
00:43:45.789 --> 00:43:48.584
You need to know
who your opponents are to fight them.

680
00:43:49.251 --> 00:43:50.085
Right?

681
00:43:52.796 --> 00:43:53.714
Never mind.

682
00:43:54.923 --> 00:43:58.177
There's no need for the staff
to do so much work.

683
00:43:59.595 --> 00:44:00.638
Just…

684
00:44:02.681 --> 00:44:05.184
reveal all the rental units. Mr. Park.

685
00:44:06.185 --> 00:44:09.355
I'm preparing the ten billion
that I promised you.

686
00:44:09.438 --> 00:44:13.192
But I need some time
to gather that much cash.

687
00:44:15.903 --> 00:44:19.156
If you reveal all the rental units.

688
00:44:20.699 --> 00:44:23.118
I could get it prepared faster.

689
00:44:32.586 --> 00:44:34.129
Did you add eggs?

690
00:44:34.755 --> 00:44:35.881
Eggs are expensive.

691
00:44:35.964 --> 00:44:37.508
There's only enough for Gyeong-buk.

692
00:44:37.591 --> 00:44:39.134
Hey. what about me?

693
00:44:39.218 --> 00:44:41.136
Elderly people need protein as well.

694
00:44:41.220 --> 00:44:42.429
I'll eat them then.

695
00:44:42.513 --> 00:44:44.348
Sure. I need carbs too.

696
00:44:44.431 --> 00:44:46.266
-You're back.
-Yes.

697
00:44:47.726 --> 00:44:48.977
Ms. Kang. you're still here.

698
00:44:50.020 --> 00:44:51.355
I'm going now.

699
00:44:51.438 --> 00:44:53.482
She must have been waiting for him.

700
00:44:53.565 --> 00:44:55.984
She must've missed him all day.

701
00:44:56.068 --> 00:44:58.487
You know I can hear you. I'm leaving now.

702
00:45:00.739 --> 00:45:01.740
Bye.

703
00:45:02.533 --> 00:45:03.575
Get home safely.

704
00:45:03.659 --> 00:45:05.369
Did you eat. Boss?

705
00:45:07.287 --> 00:45:08.539
MANAGEMENT REGULATIONS

706
00:45:12.709 --> 00:45:15.170
Ms. Kang. can you work overtime today?

707
00:45:19.007 --> 00:45:20.509
"Overtime."

708
00:45:20.592 --> 00:45:22.344
{\an8}I can't believe that sounds so sweet.

709
00:45:22.428 --> 00:45:24.263
I think my heart is working overtime.

710
00:45:25.931 --> 00:45:28.350
This is the Special Act
on Private Rental Housing.

711
00:45:28.434 --> 00:45:32.187
Paragraph 2 states you can form
a council of lessees' representatives.

712
00:45:32.271 --> 00:45:34.314
But this regulation book
was made by the developer

713
00:45:34.398 --> 00:45:36.775
when the residents first moved in.

714
00:45:36.859 --> 00:45:38.819
and it's never been revised.

715
00:45:39.862 --> 00:45:41.780
But I don't understand this part.

716
00:45:41.864 --> 00:45:44.741
This part in the regulations.

717
00:45:44.825 --> 00:45:45.826
What about this?

718
00:45:47.077 --> 00:45:48.370
A love story…

719
00:45:49.788 --> 00:45:51.623
Big Guy. what are you doing?

720
00:45:52.249 --> 00:45:53.667
Should we get them some snacks?

721
00:45:53.750 --> 00:45:54.960
It's not the time for that.

722
00:45:56.211 --> 00:45:58.130
We should give them some privacy.

723
00:45:58.714 --> 00:45:59.548
Close the door.

724
00:46:04.261 --> 00:46:05.679
What are they doing?

725
00:46:06.930 --> 00:46:08.640
-Do you need anything?
-Sorry!

726
00:46:10.642 --> 00:46:11.477
Are you okay?

727
00:46:12.561 --> 00:46:14.229
Aren't you bleeding?

728
00:46:15.355 --> 00:46:16.482
So…

729
00:46:18.775 --> 00:46:19.776
Get out!

730
00:46:20.277 --> 00:46:21.361
Forgot this.

731
00:46:22.613 --> 00:46:23.530
Seriously…

732
00:46:34.124 --> 00:46:35.334
What brings you here?

733
00:46:36.126 --> 00:46:37.336
I have something to tell you.

734
00:46:38.837 --> 00:46:39.671
Sure.

735
00:46:45.594 --> 00:46:46.428
Ms. Jang.

736
00:46:47.846 --> 00:46:49.890
I need you to quit.

737
00:46:56.772 --> 00:46:58.607
You too?

738
00:47:01.151 --> 00:47:02.819
Quit your role as Senior Secretary.

739
00:47:03.487 --> 00:47:04.613
How about managing

740
00:47:05.113 --> 00:47:07.699
apartment affairs with me
as another president?

741
00:47:09.159 --> 00:47:11.328
So with the revision
to the rental housing laws.

742
00:47:11.411 --> 00:47:13.789
tenants in rental housing complexes
with 150 or more units

743
00:47:13.872 --> 00:47:16.750
should have formed
a tenants' representative council.

744
00:47:16.833 --> 00:47:17.668
That's right.

745
00:47:17.751 --> 00:47:20.337
But there are 1.200 rental units here.

746
00:47:20.420 --> 00:47:21.880
Why hasn't one been formed?

747
00:47:23.507 --> 00:47:24.508
We can make one now.

748
00:47:25.008 --> 00:47:28.387
We're going to form
a tenants' representative council.

749
00:47:29.096 --> 00:47:32.808
There's a tenants' representative council?

750
00:47:33.475 --> 00:47:36.895
True Value's regulations don't state
anything about a tenants' council.

751
00:47:36.979 --> 00:47:39.856
I'll correct any wrong
management regulations here.

752
00:47:39.940 --> 00:47:42.192
According to the Special Act
on Public Housing

753
00:47:42.276 --> 00:47:45.279
and the Special Act
on Private Rental Housing.

754
00:47:45.862 --> 00:47:49.825
rental housing residents may also form
a representative council.

755
00:47:50.617 --> 00:47:52.160
Why don't you step up for this?

756
00:47:54.580 --> 00:47:55.414
Me?

757
00:47:55.998 --> 00:47:57.207
From now on.

758
00:47:57.291 --> 00:48:01.003
make your voice heard
as a representative of the tenants.

759
00:48:03.046 --> 00:48:04.590
President Park…

760
00:48:10.387 --> 00:48:12.681
{\an8}TENANTS' COUNCIL
BUILDING REPRESENTATIVE ELECTION

761
00:48:12.764 --> 00:48:15.684
{\an8}Mr. Park. you're smarter than I thought.

762
00:48:16.768 --> 00:48:18.353
It's all thanks to our overtime work.

763
00:48:18.437 --> 00:48:20.147
Don't forget my overtime pay.

764
00:48:24.026 --> 00:48:24.943
CANDIDATE PROFILE

765
00:48:25.027 --> 00:48:27.487
<i>Jang Suk-jin can do a great job</i>

766
00:48:27.571 --> 00:48:30.824
I'm running for tenants' representative.

767
00:48:30.907 --> 00:48:32.826
We're holding an election. Please read it.

768
00:48:32.909 --> 00:48:34.286
I'm Jang Suk-jin.

769
00:48:34.369 --> 00:48:35.412
Candidate 1. Jang Suk-jin.

770
00:48:35.495 --> 00:48:37.456
-I'm a candidate.
-A tenants' rep?

771
00:48:37.539 --> 00:48:40.959
We need tenants' representatives
to improve the apartment.

772
00:48:41.043 --> 00:48:42.586
{\an8}DON'T IGNORE THE RIGHTS
OF 1.200 HOUSEHOLDS

773
00:48:42.669 --> 00:48:44.421
{\an8}Hello. please take a look.

774
00:48:45.130 --> 00:48:46.465
We're electing tenants' reps.

775
00:48:46.548 --> 00:48:49.134
Candidate 1. Jang Suk-jin.

776
00:48:49.217 --> 00:48:50.135
You may begin.

777
00:48:53.555 --> 00:48:54.723
Hello.

778
00:48:55.641 --> 00:48:58.477
I'm Candidate 1
for building representative

779
00:48:59.144 --> 00:49:01.730
on the tenants' council. Jang Suk-jin.

780
00:49:02.314 --> 00:49:05.150
I live in a rental unit.

781
00:49:05.817 --> 00:49:08.445
I can't believe I got selected.

782
00:49:08.528 --> 00:49:11.657
<i>I'm enjoying the comfort</i>
<i>and happiness of True Value</i>

783
00:49:11.740 --> 00:49:14.451
<i>for a small amount of money.</i>

784
00:49:15.410 --> 00:49:16.578
Hello.

785
00:49:17.079 --> 00:49:19.164
It's a rental unit
managed by the government.

786
00:49:20.916 --> 00:49:24.336
<i>I understand the sense of superiority</i>
<i>that some homeowners have.</i>

787
00:49:25.379 --> 00:49:27.714
You've worked extremely hard.

788
00:49:27.798 --> 00:49:29.591
{\an8}mortgaged your futures.

789
00:49:29.675 --> 00:49:33.220
{\an8}and sacrificed other chances at happiness

790
00:49:33.303 --> 00:49:35.681
to buy your apartments.

791
00:49:37.224 --> 00:49:40.394
<i>However. I would like to ask you</i>

792
00:49:40.477 --> 00:49:44.690
to acknowledge the residents
in rental units

793
00:49:44.773 --> 00:49:47.442
{\an8}as a part of True Value's community.

794
00:49:48.193 --> 00:49:51.655
<i>We do not wish to live here</i>

795
00:49:51.738 --> 00:49:55.534
<i>as shameful parasites</i>
<i>living off True Value.</i>

796
00:49:55.617 --> 00:49:59.538
I would like to live here proudly
as a resident of a rental unit.

797
00:49:59.621 --> 00:50:02.666
enjoying my freedom
and fulfilling my responsibilities.

798
00:50:03.291 --> 00:50:04.292
Anyone here?

799
00:50:04.793 --> 00:50:05.711
Light's still on.

800
00:50:05.794 --> 00:50:08.213
<i>I will take on the responsibility</i>

801
00:50:08.296 --> 00:50:11.758
<i>of caring for and protecting</i>
<i>the facilities of this community</i>

802
00:50:11.842 --> 00:50:14.302
<i>as if they were my own.</i>

803
00:50:15.220 --> 00:50:16.513
Here.

804
00:50:18.557 --> 00:50:20.142
I. Jang Suk-jin.

805
00:50:20.684 --> 00:50:22.644
will represent the tenants

806
00:50:22.728 --> 00:50:25.522
and do my best to cooperate
with the homeowners

807
00:50:25.605 --> 00:50:29.568
to create a better environment
at True Value.

808
00:50:30.485 --> 00:50:31.486
{\an8}Thank you.

809
00:50:40.579 --> 00:50:43.415
I TOTALLY AGREE WITH YOU…
I HOPE YOU GET ELECTED!

810
00:50:45.041 --> 00:50:46.334
"I support you."

811
00:50:48.628 --> 00:50:50.338
"Thank you."

812
00:50:51.840 --> 00:50:53.133
I'm so grateful.

813
00:50:58.513 --> 00:51:01.224
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR APPOINTMENT!

814
00:51:01.308 --> 00:51:04.060
-Congratulations.
-Congratulations.

815
00:51:04.144 --> 00:51:05.562
Thank you!

816
00:51:05.645 --> 00:51:06.938
Thank you. everyone!

817
00:51:07.022 --> 00:51:08.315
Here's your certificate.

818
00:51:08.398 --> 00:51:09.900
"President Jang Suk-jin."

819
00:51:09.983 --> 00:51:13.361
"You are hereby appointed president
of the tenants' representative council."

820
00:51:13.945 --> 00:51:15.071
Congratulations.

821
00:51:15.155 --> 00:51:16.740
Thank you.

822
00:51:16.823 --> 00:51:19.701
{\an8}I got a certificate!

823
00:51:19.785 --> 00:51:21.328
{\an8}I look forward to working with you.

824
00:51:21.411 --> 00:51:23.288
{\an8}President Park!

825
00:51:23.914 --> 00:51:25.874
{\an8}I'll keep doing my best

826
00:51:25.957 --> 00:51:30.003
{\an8}to love True Value State!

827
00:51:30.086 --> 00:51:32.047
{\an8}You can love True Value a little less.

828
00:51:32.130 --> 00:51:34.966
{\an8}No. I love True Value so much.

829
00:51:35.050 --> 00:51:36.635
{\an8}Look at this. everyone.

830
00:51:37.511 --> 00:51:40.013
{\an8}Mothers. Oh my gosh.

831
00:51:40.096 --> 00:51:41.181
Hang on.

832
00:51:41.765 --> 00:51:44.726
Congratulations. President Jang.

833
00:51:46.228 --> 00:51:47.979
I'm really sorry about before.

834
00:51:48.063 --> 00:51:51.900
It's fine. I've already put it behind me.

835
00:51:52.526 --> 00:51:55.111
Let's work together from now on.

836
00:51:55.195 --> 00:51:56.112
President Jang!

837
00:51:56.196 --> 00:51:57.739
How about a photo together?

838
00:51:57.823 --> 00:51:59.324
-Gather round.
-Let's take one.

839
00:51:59.407 --> 00:52:00.450
Come here.

840
00:52:00.534 --> 00:52:02.202
All right. Oh gosh!

841
00:52:02.869 --> 00:52:03.995
What?

842
00:52:04.079 --> 00:52:05.038
President Park.

843
00:52:05.789 --> 00:52:08.792
-President Park. you should come here.
-Sorry.

844
00:52:11.461 --> 00:52:12.754
{\an8}All right. then.

845
00:52:12.838 --> 00:52:14.464
{\an8}Say "Suk-jin" on the count of three.

846
00:52:14.965 --> 00:52:15.966
{\an8}Mr. Choi!

847
00:52:16.466 --> 00:52:17.717
{\an8}One. two. three.

848
00:52:17.801 --> 00:52:19.553
-Suk-jin!
-Suk-jin!

849
00:52:19.636 --> 00:52:21.221
TENANTS' COUNCIL
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN

850
00:52:22.389 --> 00:52:27.060
Walking around our apartment complex
as a president

851
00:52:27.143 --> 00:52:30.105
feels so different.

852
00:52:33.316 --> 00:52:34.401
Damn it.

853
00:52:34.484 --> 00:52:37.028
They always throw trash
in places like this.

854
00:52:37.112 --> 00:52:38.154
Geez.

855
00:52:39.072 --> 00:52:41.908
Ms. Jang. you're a president now.

856
00:52:41.992 --> 00:52:43.952
Maybe you should watch your language…

857
00:52:44.035 --> 00:52:46.079
Oh. you're right.

858
00:52:46.162 --> 00:52:49.708
You're absolutely right.
I should be more cautious now.

859
00:52:52.168 --> 00:52:53.670
But President Park.

860
00:52:53.753 --> 00:52:55.255
I don't care

861
00:52:55.338 --> 00:52:58.216
who you used to be

862
00:52:58.300 --> 00:53:01.803
or what you did in the past anymore.

863
00:53:02.512 --> 00:53:03.346
What?

864
00:53:04.306 --> 00:53:07.392
It doesn't matter
what your intentions were

865
00:53:07.475 --> 00:53:10.562
when you created a fake family

866
00:53:11.354 --> 00:53:13.940
and became the president.

867
00:53:14.524 --> 00:53:16.610
I feel like

868
00:53:16.693 --> 00:53:21.197
you were sent from the heavens
to make this place

869
00:53:21.281 --> 00:53:23.533
a better apartment complex for us.

870
00:53:24.451 --> 00:53:26.411
Isn't that enough?

871
00:53:27.537 --> 00:53:31.499
Where have you been all this time?

872
00:53:32.584 --> 00:53:34.544
Oh gosh. Choco's owner.

873
00:53:34.628 --> 00:53:37.422
He's not cleaning up after his dog again.

874
00:53:37.505 --> 00:53:39.049
He did that last time too.

875
00:53:39.132 --> 00:53:40.091
Choco!

876
00:53:40.175 --> 00:53:41.217
Hey!

877
00:53:41.301 --> 00:53:43.762
You should clean up after your dog!

878
00:53:46.932 --> 00:53:48.516
A better place…

879
00:53:53.855 --> 00:53:55.315
A better place…

880
00:53:56.358 --> 00:53:58.818
ELECTION RESULTS

881
00:54:01.529 --> 00:54:02.781
VERIFYING MY RENTAL UNIT

882
00:54:02.864 --> 00:54:06.242
I told him to reveal the rental units.
and this is what he does?

883
00:54:06.826 --> 00:54:08.870
They're revealing themselves voluntarily.

884
00:54:08.954 --> 00:54:10.121
Does this make any sense?

885
00:54:13.041 --> 00:54:14.626
Is this

886
00:54:14.709 --> 00:54:16.378
Park Hae-kang's magic?

887
00:54:20.840 --> 00:54:22.759
This is entertaining…

888
00:54:23.802 --> 00:54:26.221
but I feel strangely uncomfortable.

889
00:54:36.147 --> 00:54:37.482
I'm home.

890
00:54:43.154 --> 00:54:44.447
I guess she's still working.

891
00:54:49.828 --> 00:54:51.579
What a mess.

892
00:55:15.895 --> 00:55:16.730
What?

893
00:55:17.522 --> 00:55:20.066
Darn it. Ha-jeong's going
to nag me about this.

894
00:55:22.444 --> 00:55:25.238
I always mess up
when I do something I usually don't do.

895
00:55:35.582 --> 00:55:36.499
What is this?

896
00:55:39.085 --> 00:55:41.713
TRANSACTION LEDGER

897
00:55:52.432 --> 00:55:54.267
PARKING GARAGE LIGHT INSPECTION
(NOT CONDUCTED)

898
00:55:54.350 --> 00:55:55.602
WALKWAY CRACK REPAIRS
(REDUCED SCOPE)

899
00:55:55.685 --> 00:55:57.520
EXTERIOR WALL CRACK INSPECTION
(NOT CONDUCTED)

900
00:55:57.604 --> 00:55:59.564
LANDSCAPE PLANTING REPAIRS
(FALSIFIED QUANTITIES)

901
00:56:23.171 --> 00:56:24.047
You…

902
00:56:27.217 --> 00:56:28.426
How did you…

903
00:56:28.510 --> 00:56:30.637
Is this what you were doing
in the management office?

904
00:56:32.972 --> 00:56:34.974
What the hell have you been doing?

905
00:56:37.310 --> 00:56:38.561
It's nothing.

906
00:56:39.062 --> 00:56:40.021
You don't need to know.

907
00:56:40.105 --> 00:56:41.356
It's not nothing.

908
00:56:41.439 --> 00:56:43.525
You supported me
with money you earned like this?

909
00:56:43.608 --> 00:56:44.567
With filthy money?

910
00:56:44.651 --> 00:56:46.611
What's filthy about money?

911
00:56:46.694 --> 00:56:48.488
There's no such thing as filthy money.

912
00:56:48.571 --> 00:56:49.572
Money is just money.

913
00:56:50.198 --> 00:56:51.074
Kang Ha-jeong.

914
00:56:51.658 --> 00:56:55.120
What else could I have done. then?

915
00:56:55.203 --> 00:56:59.040
How could I pay for law school tuition
with my salary?

916
00:56:59.958 --> 00:57:01.751
You said you earned a lot.

917
00:57:01.835 --> 00:57:03.920
You said you had a good salary!

918
00:57:04.003 --> 00:57:06.464
So this is why you were earning a lot.

919
00:57:06.548 --> 00:57:09.467
It was stupid of me to believe you!

920
00:57:10.426 --> 00:57:13.429
You don't need to worry about this.
I'm handling this on my own.

921
00:57:13.513 --> 00:57:14.639
Stop this. right now.

922
00:57:14.722 --> 00:57:17.600
Do you even know
what you've gotten yourself into?

923
00:57:18.184 --> 00:57:20.520
I just did as I was told.

924
00:57:21.271 --> 00:57:22.522
and I was paid for it.

925
00:57:23.273 --> 00:57:24.691
Ha-jeong!

926
00:57:25.191 --> 00:57:28.987
Have you lost your mind? Kang Ha-jeong!

927
00:57:29.696 --> 00:57:30.697
No…

928
00:57:30.780 --> 00:57:33.575
I was the one who was crazy
for eating. sleeping.

929
00:57:33.658 --> 00:57:35.452
and studying with that money.

930
00:57:55.138 --> 00:57:56.848
Mr. Choi…

931
00:57:57.599 --> 00:57:59.267
I'm really sorry.

932
00:58:00.602 --> 00:58:02.353
but I can't do this any longer.

933
00:58:03.771 --> 00:58:05.690
I'm really going to quit now.

934
00:58:05.773 --> 00:58:07.484
So tell Mr. Lee for me.

935
00:58:09.736 --> 00:58:10.778
Ha-jeong.

936
00:58:13.656 --> 00:58:15.533
If you can't do this.

937
00:58:16.159 --> 00:58:18.870
you can accept Mr. Lee's offer.

938
00:58:19.370 --> 00:58:21.998
No. I don't need that.

939
00:58:23.875 --> 00:58:25.210
Let's not do this.

940
00:58:26.377 --> 00:58:27.712
This

941
00:58:27.795 --> 00:58:30.548
could be a matter
of life and death for us.

942
00:58:32.050 --> 00:58:34.177
I'm telling you. I can't do this.

943
00:58:34.844 --> 00:58:36.846
I'm going to pretend I didn't hear this.

944
00:58:38.973 --> 00:58:40.767
I have a ledger.

945
00:58:44.187 --> 00:58:45.063
Ha-jeong.

946
00:58:46.523 --> 00:58:49.317
I recorded everything we've done so far.

947
00:58:54.113 --> 00:58:54.948
If…

948
00:58:56.032 --> 00:58:57.242
If you let me quit.

949
00:58:57.325 --> 00:58:58.952
I'll get rid of the ledger

950
00:58:59.035 --> 00:59:01.204
and live quietly for the rest of my life.

951
00:59:07.377 --> 00:59:09.420
Ha-jeong!

952
00:59:28.064 --> 00:59:31.067
PRESIDENT LEE CHUNG-WON

953
00:59:38.491 --> 00:59:39.409
I…

954
00:59:40.285 --> 00:59:41.911
There's an emergency. sir.

955
00:59:47.041 --> 00:59:49.544
She has a handwritten ledger?

956
00:59:49.627 --> 00:59:50.628
Unbelievable.

957
00:59:51.379 --> 00:59:55.508
So is she thinking of blackmailing me?

958
00:59:57.844 --> 01:00:00.972
She's quite crafty. isn't she?

959
01:00:01.055 --> 01:00:03.600
I really had no idea. sir.

960
01:00:04.642 --> 01:00:07.562
But it doesn't seem
like she has any ill intentions.

961
01:00:08.062 --> 01:00:10.773
If you just allow her to quit…

962
01:00:11.482 --> 01:00:13.109
I can't just leave her be.

963
01:00:13.192 --> 01:00:15.737
She said she'd live quietly if she quit.

964
01:00:15.820 --> 01:00:17.071
And she's trustworthy.

965
01:00:21.909 --> 01:00:24.078
You're so naive. Mr. Choi.

966
01:00:25.496 --> 01:00:26.414
Pardon?

967
01:00:27.165 --> 01:00:30.209
She's been preparing this meticulously
for a long time.

968
01:00:31.628 --> 01:00:33.630
How can you trust someone

969
01:00:33.713 --> 01:00:36.382
who's holding a huge missile in her arms?

970
01:00:38.384 --> 01:00:39.302
She…

971
01:00:39.385 --> 01:00:40.303
She's been

972
01:00:41.304 --> 01:00:43.181
cooperative until now.

973
01:00:44.140 --> 01:00:45.975
She's only asking to quit.

974
01:00:47.226 --> 01:00:48.353
We can trust her.

975
01:00:50.146 --> 01:00:51.022
You know…

976
01:00:52.899 --> 01:00:55.610
I really hate having to wear wet shoes.

977
01:00:56.402 --> 01:00:58.821
not being able to wash my hands
after using the bathroom.

978
01:00:59.906 --> 01:01:03.242
not being able to shower
after working out.

979
01:01:03.326 --> 01:01:04.994
things like that.

980
01:01:05.078 --> 01:01:06.954
I really despise that feeling.

981
01:01:07.955 --> 01:01:09.666
It makes me feel really uneasy.

982
01:01:09.749 --> 01:01:10.750
But right now.

983
01:01:10.833 --> 01:01:13.294
Kang Ha-jeong is making me feel that way.

984
01:01:13.378 --> 01:01:15.254
I feel uneasy.

985
01:01:17.590 --> 01:01:21.010
I feel so uneasy!

986
01:01:23.304 --> 01:01:26.724
ACCOUNTING MANAGER
KANG HA-JEONG

987
01:01:32.689 --> 01:01:33.523
Hey.

988
01:01:34.148 --> 01:01:35.191
Join me.

989
01:01:37.068 --> 01:01:38.903
Come on. Join me.

990
01:01:39.404 --> 01:01:41.781
It's boring doing this alone. Come on.

991
01:01:44.158 --> 01:01:45.118
Sure.

992
01:01:56.379 --> 01:01:58.965
What do you do when you get a hangnail.

993
01:01:59.048 --> 01:02:00.466
Mr. Park?

994
01:02:01.259 --> 01:02:04.011
Do you tear it off. or just leave it?

995
01:02:06.264 --> 01:02:07.098
I tear it off.

996
01:02:08.266 --> 01:02:09.809
I knew it.

997
01:02:09.892 --> 01:02:12.979
I tear it off. even if I start bleeding.
It makes me uneasy.

998
01:02:16.441 --> 01:02:18.025
Can you do something for me?

999
01:02:18.985 --> 01:02:20.236
What is it?

1000
01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:23.322
Mr. Kim will contact you later tonight.

1001
01:02:23.406 --> 01:02:26.075
It's nothing special.
You just need to drive.

1002
01:02:26.159 --> 01:02:29.495
Just get in the car
and drive when I tell you to.

1003
01:02:29.579 --> 01:02:31.622
and stop when I tell you to stop.

1004
01:02:31.706 --> 01:02:32.790
It will be easy.

1005
01:02:34.459 --> 01:02:35.668
And when it's over.

1006
01:02:36.669 --> 01:02:38.337
I'll give you the ten billion.

1007
01:02:49.974 --> 01:02:51.184
I'll count on you. then.

1008
01:03:07.658 --> 01:03:09.994
Start the engine and wait inside.

1009
01:03:10.077 --> 01:03:11.496
He'll call you.

1010
01:03:41.234 --> 01:03:42.652
This is Park Hae-kang.

1011
01:03:42.735 --> 01:03:44.362
<i>Yes. I know.</i>

1012
01:03:44.445 --> 01:03:46.864
Of course. I recognize your voice.

1013
01:03:46.948 --> 01:03:49.367
Did you start the car?

1014
01:03:50.076 --> 01:03:50.952
Yes.

1015
01:03:51.536 --> 01:03:52.662
<i>All right.</i>

1016
01:03:52.745 --> 01:03:56.916
Now accelerate gently
and head out onto the main road.

1017
01:04:17.061 --> 01:04:18.521
<i>Good.</i>

1018
01:04:19.146 --> 01:04:20.439
<i>Go straight.</i>

1019
01:04:20.523 --> 01:04:22.441
then turn left into the main road.

1020
01:04:23.442 --> 01:04:25.570
Okay. Turning left.

1021
01:04:30.783 --> 01:04:33.411
Good. You're a good driver.

1022
01:04:34.453 --> 01:04:36.581
It's almost over.

1023
01:04:43.421 --> 01:04:45.214
SHOULD WE HAVE SPICY RICE CAKES LATER?

1024
01:04:48.301 --> 01:04:52.722
<i>Why don't you start</i>
<i>increasing the speed now?</i>

1025
01:05:02.023 --> 01:05:05.902
<i>There's going to be a bus stop</i>
<i>about 300 meters in front of you.</i>

1026
01:05:05.985 --> 01:05:07.403
<i>Do you see it?</i>

1027
01:05:07.486 --> 01:05:08.529
Yes. I see it.

1028
01:05:08.613 --> 01:05:10.406
Crash into the woman

1029
01:05:10.489 --> 01:05:12.283
{\an8}standing there!

1030
01:06:07.171 --> 01:06:08.422
Park Hae-kang…

1031
01:06:12.218 --> 01:06:13.219
All right.

1032
01:06:13.886 --> 01:06:15.388
I'm coming to you.

1033
01:06:36.993 --> 01:06:38.119
This is ten billion won.

1034
01:06:38.953 --> 01:06:41.664
I told you I'd give you the money
once you did this.

1035
01:06:42.248 --> 01:06:44.792
You can save your old boss
with this money.

1036
01:06:44.875 --> 01:06:47.753
You shouldn't leave him there
when he's already sick.

1037
01:06:48.379 --> 01:06:50.339
All you had to do

1038
01:06:50.423 --> 01:06:52.633
was crash into a woman
standing right there.

1039
01:06:53.259 --> 01:06:54.969
You've pulled off harder things than that.

1040
01:06:55.052 --> 01:06:58.305
but you fail to do the easiest job?

1041
01:07:00.224 --> 01:07:01.809
I may be a bad guy.

1042
01:07:02.685 --> 01:07:04.353
but you're just trash.

1043
01:07:04.937 --> 01:07:06.439
Trash?

1044
01:07:07.189 --> 01:07:10.317
You're being quite rude to a guy

1045
01:07:11.485 --> 01:07:12.737
who's interested in you.

1046
01:07:13.571 --> 01:07:15.239
I don't date trash.

1047
01:07:18.075 --> 01:07:20.286
Then what will you do with me?

1048
01:07:21.203 --> 01:07:22.413
I think

1049
01:07:23.122 --> 01:07:25.583
I can make things
very interesting for you.

1050
01:07:36.093 --> 01:07:38.804
THE APARTMENT JOB

1051
01:08:02.912 --> 01:08:05.456
{\an8}I would like to suggest a safety patrol.

1052
01:08:05.539 --> 01:08:08.375
{\an8}<i>We should show everyone</i>
<i>that we're the ones</i>

1053
01:08:08.459 --> 01:08:11.295
{\an8}<i>who care the most about this place.</i>

1054
01:08:11.378 --> 01:08:13.089
{\an8}Goodness. What is all this?

1055
01:08:13.172 --> 01:08:14.715
{\an8}<i>That's Gyeong-buk's kindergarten.</i>

1056
01:08:14.799 --> 01:08:16.425
{\an8}<i>President Park. we need you to step up.</i>

1057
01:08:16.509 --> 01:08:18.135
{\an8}<i>Of course.</i>
<i>I should step up as the president.</i>

1058
01:08:18.219 --> 01:08:21.097
{\an8}Has the building really aged this fast?

1059
01:08:21.180 --> 01:08:22.765
{\an8}No. it's shoddy construction.

1060
01:08:22.848 --> 01:08:24.809
{\an8}<i>President Park's wife?</i>

1061
01:08:24.892 --> 01:08:26.769
{\an8}<i>So it's you. You tried to kill my sister.</i>

1062
01:08:26.852 --> 01:08:28.020
{\an8}<i>How about 500 million?</i>

1063
01:08:28.104 --> 01:08:30.856
{\an8}I'm sure that's more than what you got
for playing Park Hae-kang's wife.

1064
01:08:30.940 --> 01:08:32.066
{\an8}<i>If you want him released…</i>

1065
01:08:32.149 --> 01:08:33.734
{\an8}<i>Police! Open the door.</i>

1066
01:08:33.818 --> 01:08:35.402
{\an8}<i>…bring me the ledger.</i>

1067
01:08:35.486 --> 01:08:37.113
{\an8}Simple. isn't it?

1068
01:08:37.196 --> 01:08:40.282
{\an8}<i>It's not something you can handle.</i>
<i>Hand it over to me.</i>

1069
01:08:40.366 --> 01:08:41.659
{\an8}<i>I can't hand it over.</i>

1070
01:08:44.703 --> 01:08:46.705
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

